@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted	GO:query
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:240
@SQ	SN:chr2	LN:240
@CO	05-drops-promotion-readthrough.
@CO	sup_inside_overlap: molecule chr1:21-90(+) | chr2:41-60(+) | chr1:141-210(+), L=160, reads 100/100, overlap f[60,100). R2 MAPQ 30 everywhere, so R1 keeps.
@CO	sup_inside_overlap: R2 = primary chr1:141-210 (rev) + supplementary chr2:41-60 (rev, f70-89) + supplementary chr1:81-90 (rev, f60-69). Both R2 supplementaries lie wholly inside the overlap.
@CO	primary_inside_overlap: molecule chr2:141-160(+) | chr1:41-120(+), L=100, reads 80/80, overlap f[20,80). The aligner chose R1's chr1 segment (f20-79, MAPQ 20) as PRIMARY 20S60M and the chr2 segment (f0-19) as supplementary 20M60H.
@CO	primary_inside_overlap: R2 (MAPQ 60) keeps; R1's primary lies wholly inside the overlap.
@CO	read_through: 30 bp molecule chr1:161-190 read with 40 bp reads; the 10 adapter bases (AGATCGGAAG) are soft-clipped on both reads. L=30 < read length.
@CO	read_through_aligned: 30 bp molecule chr2:161-190, but R1's 10 bases past the molecule end aligned (40M to chr2:161-200) instead of soft-clipping.
@CO	adapter_indel: as read_through_aligned (30 bp molecule chr2:161-190), but R1 is 37M1I2M: its aligned read-through carries a 1-base insertion 2 bases from its 3' end, i.e. inside the adapter.
